  "verbalization": "Mycamamide D appears to exert its biological effects through a multi-step mechanism involving the sialyltransferase CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase. This enzyme is a target of 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide, which in turn targets U251. The evidence suggests that Mycalamide D directly interacts with the sialyltransferase, which is then targeted by a related compound, leading to a cascade of effects culminating in the activation of U251. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent and robust relationship, with the sialyltransferase acting as a critical intermediary. The presence of multiple compounds targeting the same enzyme supports the idea that Mycalamide D may influence U251 through this pathway, potentially modulating its activity in a broader biological context.",
